# React Frontend Conventions

You are a senior React developer focused on scalable, maintainable, accessible applications.

**Precedence:** `adonisjswithreact.mdc` and `inertia-no-direct-injection.mdc` always win over this file. Where this file conflicts with them or with established codebase patterns, follow the existing rules and patterns.

## Style Guide

- Be direct and concise, no unnecessary explanations
- Do not add comments unless requested
- Simplicity first: clarity and consistency over cleverness
- Use subtle micro-interactions on interactive elements; animations enhance, never distract
- Respect the design system and existing component patterns
- Prioritize UX and follow modern React best practices

## Tech Stack (actual)

| Concern | Use | Do not introduce |
|---|---|---|
| UI | React 19 functional components + hooks | Class components (except error boundaries) |
| Routing / navigation | Inertia (`router.visit`, `<Link>` from `@inertiajs/react`) | React Router |
| Server state | TanStack Query via `_hooks.ts` + `http()` | SWR, ad-hoc `fetch` in components |
| Validation / types | Zod schemas in `_types.ts`, `z.infer` | Inline schemas |
| Forms | `inertia/components/form/*` + `inertia/lib/form.ts` helpers + `useMutation` | React Hook Form, Inertia `useForm` for API mutations |
| Client state | `useState` / `useReducer` / Context | Zustand (ask first; only if cross-page client state is genuinely needed) |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 utilities (`@tailwindcss/vite`), theme tokens in `inertia/css/app.css` | New BEM/custom CSS classes, CSS-in-JS, shadcn/ui (ask first) |
| Icons / toasts | `lucide-react`, `sonner` | Other icon/toast libraries |
| Build | Vite via `@adonisjs/vite` | Separate Vite/Webpack configs |
| Tests | Japa (`@japa/runner`, `@japa/browser-client`) | Vitest, Jest, Cypress (ask first) |

Never add a dependency without asking. Use `yarn`.

## Code Conventions

- **File naming:** snake_case (`form_input_number.tsx`, `query_client.ts`). Page-private files start with `_` (`_hooks.ts`, `_types.ts`)
- `*.tsx` for components, `*.ts` for hooks, utilities, schemas and config
- **Default exports** for components and pages; **named exports** for hooks, utilities, schemas and types
- **Import order:**
  1. React and React-related (`react`, `@inertiajs/react`)
  2. Third-party libraries (`@tanstack/react-query`, `zod`, `lucide-react`)
  3. Internal aliases (`~/lib/*`, `~/components/*`)
  4. Relative imports
- **Code style** (enforced by `@adonisjs/prettier-config`): single quotes, 2-space indent, no semicolons, no trailing whitespace
- Prefer `const`, template strings, optional chaining (`?.`) and nullish coalescing (`??`)

## Styling (Tailwind CSS v4)

- Style with Tailwind utility classes in `className`; no new custom CSS classes and no inline `style` (except truly dynamic values)
- Use the project's semantic theme colors, never raw hex or Tailwind palette colors: `bg-paper`, `bg-card`, `text-ink`, `text-ink-2`, `text-muted`, `text-subtle`, `border-line`, `border-line-2`, `bg-btn`/`text-btn-fg`, `bg-field`, `ring-ring`, `text-ok`, `text-danger`. Fonts: `font-sans` (Inter, self-hosted via `@fontsource-variable/inter`), `font-mono`, `font-serif`. Never load fonts from Google Fonts or other CDNs. Card radius: `rounded-card`
- Add new tokens in `inertia/css/app.css`: the raw value in `:root` and `:root[data-theme='dark']`, then map it in `@theme inline` as `--color-*`
- Dark mode is driven by `data-theme` on `<html>`; tokens switch automatically, and the `dark:` variant is available for one-off overrides
- Reuse shared class helpers from `inertia/lib/styles.ts` (`cn`, `buttonClasses`, `iconButton`, `field`, `panel`, `table`, `tag`, `inlineLink`, `auth`) before writing new long class strings; add a helper there when a pattern repeats in 2+ places
- Style links that look like buttons with `buttonClasses({ variant, size })`
- Focus states: `focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-3 focus-visible:ring-ring`
- Animations use `motion-safe:` so `prefers-reduced-motion` is respected
- Plain CSS in `app.css` is only for base styles and third-party overrides that must beat unlayered library CSS (e.g. Sonner)

## React Patterns

- Functional components with hooks; extract reusable logic into custom hooks
- Composition over inheritance; compound components for complex UI
- Single responsibility per component; avoid prop drilling (lift into a hook or Context)
- Render props / children-as-function only when composition alone is insufficient
- Error boundaries around page sections that can fail independently
- Keep components feature-based: page-specific components live next to the page; shared ones go in `inertia/components/`

## Component Library

Reusable UI lives in one library. Check it before writing new markup, and import from the folder barrels:

```typescript
import { Avatar, Badge, Checkbox, IconButton, SearchInput, Select, Skeleton } from '~/components/ui'
import { DataTable, DataTableToolbar, InfiniteDataTable, type DataTableColumn } from '~/components/data_table'
import { FormButton, FormCheckbox, FormInput, FormInputNumber, FormSelect } from '~/components/form'
```

| Folder | Holds |
|---|---|
| `components/ui/` | Presentational primitives without label/error wiring |
| `components/form/` | Labelled form fields built on `ui/` primitives |
| `components/data_table/` | The presentation-only table, toolbar, footer and pager |

- Library components are domain-agnostic: no `http()`, TanStack Query, Inertia routes, or page `_hooks`/`_types` imports, and no record types such as `AdminUser`.
- `DataTable` only renders the `rows` and `columns` it receives. Sorting and selection are controlled props plus callbacks; the page owns that state (`useListQueryState` in `~/hooks/`) and fetches the rows. Domain cells (badges, avatars, formatted dates) belong in the page's `columns` config.
- Back-office list pages load rows in batches of 25: add a `useAdmin<Resource>Infinite(filters)` hook built on `useAdminInfiniteList` (`~/hooks/use_admin_infinite_list`) and render `<InfiniteDataTable list={list} errorMessage="…" />`. It handles the loading and error states and loads the next batch when its footer scrolls into view. Don't add page-number pagination to list pages.
- Paginated list responses use `paginatedResponse(ItemSchema)` from `~/lib/schemas`; build query strings with `toQueryString()` from `~/lib/query_string`. On the backend, list validators use `listQuerySchema(sortKeys)` from `#validators/helpers/list_query`.
- Add every new library component to its folder's `index.ts`. Move a page-local component into the library once a second page needs it.

## TypeScript

- Type component props explicitly (`type XProps = ...` or `interface`), extending native element attributes where relevant (see `FormButton`)
- Use generics for reusable components; union types for variants (`'primary' | 'secondary' | 'ghost'`)
- No `any`; use `unknown` and narrow, or derive types from Zod
- Use utility types (`Pick`, `Omit`, `Partial`, `ComponentProps`)
- Keep strict mode; `yarn typecheck` must pass

## TanStack Query

- All server state goes through TanStack Query hooks in `_hooks.ts`
- Query keys are hierarchical arrays (`['admin', 'products', 'list', filters]`, `['admin', 'products', id]`)
- Invalidate by key prefix after mutations; never rely on Inertia props for records
- Use optimistic updates with rollback in `onError` where the UX benefits
- Use `useInfiniteQuery` or paginated queries with `meta` for long lists
- Prefetch (`queryClient.prefetchQuery`) on hover/intent for likely next views
- Global defaults live in `inertia/lib/query_client.ts`

## Performance

- Measure before optimizing; `React.memo`, `useMemo` and `useCallback` only for proven or obviously expensive cases
- Code-split heavy, rarely used UI with `React.lazy` + `Suspense`
- Virtualize very large lists
- Lazy-load below-the-fold images (`loading="lazy"`, explicit `width`/`height`)

## Loading States

- Handle `isLoading`, `isError` and `data` explicitly in every query consumer
- Skeletons for content areas; spinners only for quick inline operations
- Buttons show pending state via `FormButton`'s `loading` / `loadingText`
- Keep stale data visible while refetching (stale-while-revalidate)
- Prioritize above-the-fold content

## Error Handling

- Use `HttpError` from `inertia/lib/http.ts`; map 422 field errors with `zodFieldErrors()` / `handleMutationError()`
- Show user-friendly messages (no stack traces or raw server text); use `sonner` toasts for non-field errors
- Field-specific validation messages next to the field
- Provide fallback UI for failed sections and a retry action (`refetch`)
- Wrap async logic in `try/catch` where it isn't already handled by `useMutation`

## Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)

- Semantic HTML first (`button`, `nav`, `main`, `label`, `table`); ARIA only when semantics are insufficient
- Every input has an associated label; errors linked via `aria-describedby`
- Full keyboard navigation with visible focus (`ring-ring`)
- Sufficient color contrast in both light and dark themes
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for animations

## Security

- Validate input on the client (Zod) and the server (Vine)
- Never use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with user content
- CSRF is handled by Shield; always mutate through `http()` so `X-XSRF-TOKEN` is sent
- Never expose secrets in frontend code; only `VITE_`-prefixed env vars reach the client
- Validate file uploads on both sides (type, size, content)
- Auth is session-based with secure cookies; never store tokens in `localStorage`

## Testing

- Follow `adonisjswithreact.mdc`: Japa, functional tests in `tests/functional/`, unit tests in `tests/unit/`, and always ask before creating tests
- Use `@japa/browser-client` for user-flow tests when UI behavior needs coverage
